t run the rest of the suite or the frontend checks, since the spec only listed those two commands.\n\nAll changes are in `src/sensei_top/metagame/topdeck.py`:\n- **Name filter:** `_NOT_CONSTRUCTED_RE` is the regex from the spec, placed after `MAX_AGE_SECONDS`.\n- **Fetch:** `refresh_topdeck` logs a warning and adds one to `skipped` for each matching tournament. It does this right after the \"no TID\" skip.\n- **Purge:** `_purge_not_constructed(conn)` runs after `store_events`. For each stored match it clears `duplicate_of` on rows pointing at it, then deletes its rows from the four tables the spec names. It does this in one transaction with rollback on error, and logs one warning with the count. It does nothing when no stored event matches.\n\nI haven't done the \"verify against reality\" run from `CLAUDE.md` (ingest and project into a scratch database). I also haven't run `scripts/privacy_scan.py` or committed anything.", "ttft_ms": 2027, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 19846, "uuid": "38b782cf-698a-41a1-afa6-44080fa4af07", "ttft_stream_ms": 1207, "time_to_request_ms": 52, "first_content_frame_ms": 1207, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
